# tools/ IS tracked. It holds the checks that run against built-site/app.html before a
# commit, and they are no use to anyone if they live on one laptop: the biggest gap in
# this project is that most verification was never saved. Nothing in there is sensitive.
# It reads app.html, which is already public. Keep it that way: no keys, no contact
# details, no tenant ids in tools/.

# Working data drops at the repo root (xlsx, scratch exports). NOT built-site/data/,
# which is the live map data and IS tracked. Leading slash anchors this to the root.
/data/
